terse              11/12  92%
     What was total revenue in 2024 Q3?               chose search, wanted query
written properly   12/12  100%

A modest difference, and an honest one: one question in twelve.

The failure is the interesting part. With a terse description, 'What was total
revenue in 2024 Q3?' went to the document search — and that is not unreasonable,
because a quarterly review does discuss revenue. What the written description
adds is the sentence that settles it: 'do NOT use for numbers that must be
exact — those come from query'.

Two things follow. Name tools well: the first version of this listing used names
like query_warehouse, and both conditions scored 100% because the names were
doing the work. And when two tools overlap, write the 'do NOT use for' clause,
because that is the half that disambiguates and the half everyone omits.
